{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>ויענך.</b> By way of affliction." "<b>וירעיבך.</b> Either before the manna came, or in the manna itself, because it was light upon their stomach [lit. heart]; and this is not possible. But it is possible [to refer to] craving after other things." "<b>ידעון.</b> [A form] with nun [suffixed]; and likewise יקון, לחש, and also ויחנון at the crossing of Arnon." "<b>הודיעך.</b> Hiphil." "<b>הלחם.</b> [Bread] with which a person is continual." "<b>מוצא פי ה'.</b> Like 'what He decreed,' as in 'the matter went out from the mouth of the king.' And the meaning: for on bread alone does man not live, but rather by the power — or with the power — that comes from the supernal beings through the commandments of HaShem. And this is the meaning of 'מוצא פי השם.' And the proof: you did not eat bread and yet lived."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {2 "The list of forms with suffixed nun is given tersely; Ibn Ezra appears to be citing parallel examples of the nun suffix without full grammatical labels."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:50.143930383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}